  "reproduction_readme": "Windows Python 3.14.3; pure Python structlog with the task's pinned test dependencies, including Rich. No container or external runtime service. Create a fresh venv, install verification/acceptance-r1/runtime-requirements.txt and install the exact product source with pip install --no-deps -e . . Put the product src directory, product root and verification/acceptance-r1 on PYTHONPATH. Confirm structlog.__file__ and structlog.tracebacks.__file__ refer to the exact source.\n\nRun python -B -m pytest -q -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider --tb=short verification/acceptance-r1/test_locals_contract.py: 13 pass. These exercise Rich enabled/disabled; extract, transformer and real ExceptionRenderer+JSONRenderer; cause/context/nested groups; mutable caller configuration; suppressed and hidden frames; ordinary defaults. The secret object's representation protocols count and raise if touched; selected names retain <redacted> and counters stay empty. Pattern matching is case-insensitive glob matching.\n\nRun the same pytest command for tests/test_tracebacks.py: 72 pass. Run it for tests: 912 pass, 21 skip. The traceback results overlap the package suite; do not add the counts. Existing optional/platform skips remain recorded rather than presented as passes. Original native final regression also reports 912 pass and 21 skip; native lines 693-694 bind actual lint and pytest commands/results. The implementation freezes the caller pattern sequence and applies the same redactor to all exception branches before rendering. Only selected local names are protected: exception text itself is intentionally not a content-secret scanner, as documented.\n\nlog-privacy-demo.py is a separate verification helper invoking the frozen source; it is not an application UI made by the model. The delivered 75-second, continuous 1280x720 video runs the helper, independent contract and delivered traceback tests. Recorded exits are all zero. Initial r1 recording had terminal repaint corruption at frame 43 and was retained/excluded; r2 was rerecorded without editing or hiding output. Product source and native trajectory are unchanged.",
